{
  "id": "T-SHOPDAY-PAPER",
  "title": "BATCH-26 FOLD 3: the same three game hours of the client-owned GYM, crossed by ONE consensus skip. The paper simulator bills the occupied shop; a shopper who walks out unpaid is handed back to it (H-SKIPWALKIN-1). The run asserts the ACCOUNTING IDENTITY on the owner's machine. NO save.",
  "preconditions": "Reporter fixture session fx-hq1 (day 44, MERGED - vars.keepMerger true). Dev build with skipvote / skipstate / shopday / employees / schedcount / tilldupes / perf / skippace / enterbuilding / exitbuilding (BAMP_DEV). THE SHOP IS THE GYM at vars.shop, picked by t-shopday-pick: of the four player-owned customer shops it had by far the most shopper entries for the measured morning (gym 203, fast food 137, hairdresser 74, clothing 40, read on each shop's OWNING machine). ITS OWNER IS THE CLIENT, so Client1's machine runs its live customers and its till and is the machine whose numbers matter; the host stands inside the same gym and waits. The fixture loads at 17:38 with Client1 already inside a building, so both step outside for a setup skip to 10:45 the next morning - that skip is taken OUTDOORS, with no shop occupied. BATCH-26 FOLD 3: the LIVE skip-shop mode and its lever are deleted, so there is no mode to set; the paper simulator is the accountant during every skip. The owner's row now also carries the ACCOUNTING IDENTITY (idDue = idBilled + idFloor + idNosale + idCapDrop + idUnbilled, with idUnbilled 0), the H-SKIPWALKIN-1 hand-back counters, and the fold-3 measurements (visit length in game minutes, follower puppet lag, the churn counters). NOTHING IS SAVED. ORACLE NOTE: the NullReferenceException oracle carries the `(?<!swallowed )` lookbehind (as t-skippace-watch does) because fx-hq1 prints the mod's own '[Gley] swallowed NullReferenceException' traffic-collider diagnostic, which has nothing to do with this fold.",
  "instances": 2,
  "vars": {
    "clientPid": "Client1",
    "hostPid": "melaus",
    "session": "fx-hq1",
    "keepMerger": true,
    "shop": "60 ba:street_fifthavenue"
  },
  "oracles_absent": [
    "\\[TickIso\\]",
    "\\[Guard\\]",
    "(?<!swallowed )NullReferenceException"
  ],
  "oracles_report": [
    "\\[Rest\\] CONSENSUS",
    "\\[Rest\\] skip GOAL reached",
    "\\[SkipPace\\] ",
    "\\[CarStack\\] ",
    "\\[Customers\\] ",
    "\\[Perf/"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "host",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "join",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
